 change the DNA  code in the two twins referred to as  Lula and Nana as its name suggests the  CRISPR caste 9 mythology is dependent on  two  parts crisper and cast night crisper is  a kind of repeating DNA structure that  was first discovered accidentally in  bacterial DNA by Japanese scientists  Yoshizumi Asano in 1987 for 17 years  following this discovery the exact  function of these DNA repeats went  undiscovered until it was identified as  the means by which bacteria identify and  protect themselves against invading  viral DNA it turned out these strange  DNA repeats actually came from viruses  bacteria have the ability to cut up  invading viral DNA store it in their own  DNA and then subsequently use it as a  guide system for the enzymes cast 9  which destroys the viral DNA sequence  should it invade again in the future in  order to do this cast 9 uses the stored  DNA to make something called the guide  RNA this guide RNA is usually coded for  by a CRISPR repeat and guides CRISPR to  DNA it should cut there are two  conditions for CRISPR is binding to its  target first caste 9 must bind to the  target sequence and a specific 3 code  variation in DNA which is called a pom  most poms can be recognized by caste 9  as they contain the code GG these  reoccurring patterns are targeted by a  bacterias caste 9 system as they  identify the DNA of invading viruses  this gives the bacteria an ability to  target and destroy the viral DNA however  in the last five years we've learned to  leverage this ability to direct cast  night with guide RNAs of our own design  to alter the genome of other organisms  the guide RNA binds to a parent of caste  9 called the alpha helical lobe in turn  another domain of caste 9 the nucleus  lobe binds to an e flanking part of the  DNA strands that matches with the guide  RNA causing the double helix structure  of the DNA to unwind this process is  facilitated by the proximity between the  DNA and the caste 9 complex and  electrostatic interactions that occur  between the RNA and DNA at this point  two specific domains of the nucleus lobe  cut the DNA although we're not fully  sure how this mechanism occurs  comparative studies suggest the most  likely way is that the two separate  parts of caste 9 are able to rip protons  from water molecules and in turn  weaponize a''s the deprotonated water  molecule to break the DNA apart this is  done at two sites in the DNA one which  Cleaves the DNA at the target site and  another which cleaves the DNA at a non  target site at this point a number of  things can happen depending on which  approach is needed cast 9 can be  modified to include a deaminase enzyme  which can target specific basis for  mutation leading to brand-new mutations  a process known as homology directed  repair can be used to insert new DNA at  the coding site or the targeted piece of  DNA can be simply cut out and removed if  it is deemed to be undesirable dr.  Hirsch Inc we opted for the later option  and simply cut a section of a gene  called ccr5 the section that was cut  corresponding to a mutation known as  Delta 32 that confers its owner with  protection to certain strands of HIV  doctor whose data seems to suggest he  may have artificially induced a mutation  similar to but not identical to the  Delta 32 mutation in these twins in  order to do this dr. hood had to first  optimize the gene editing protocol in  mice monkey and human cells the reason  for this is to make sure the protocol  has high specificity simply put that the  gene editing technique was editing the  target DNA and not some other sequence  this claim is of course key to the  validity of the experiment on edited  embryos can be thrown away after all but  for obvious reasons making on specific  alterations to a human's genetic code  would be a major red flag and dr. his  work raises major red flags for this  exact reason there check for specificity  of gene editing use parental genetics as  a reference point an inadequate approach  due to the fact that a parent's genetic  material is subject to a certain degree  of randomization every time a sperm or  egg is produced it's further complicated  by the fact that no two sperm or eggs  will be the same and that their  mythology did not account for the  possibility that larger sections of the  genetic code  could be deleted by their implementation  of the CRISPR caste 9 system further to  this from the data released so far we  can tell that the mutation induced in  the twins does not exactly mirror the  Delta 32 population that her is  attempting to induce in the twins  although the protein produced should in  theory largely mirror the naturally  occurring mutation we cannot tell that  for sure because it has not been tested  standard practice at this point is to  test these mutations in an animal model  in order to assess unexpected effects of  the experiment this is perhaps the most  troublesome part of this experiment Lulu  and Nana are test subjects for a genetic  mutation that we have not even taken the  time or care to test in animals  nonetheless the mutation was induced in  a total of 31 human embryos these  embryos were grown for a period of five  to eight days and the 19 that were  deemed normal were taken forward out of  these 19 embryos two were implanted in  the mother to give rise to the twins  these concerns over Lulu and Nana's  well-being are only one of a myriad of  issues perhaps most critically there was  no medical need for this treatment in  the first place it has been claimed that  the biological father of the twins is  HIV positive but given that the couple  used IVF and that there is no evidence  that HIV would be passed on from father  to child using this method of conception  the procedure was medically unnecessary  furthermore her claims to have induced  this mutation completely into at least  one of the twins to do this her and his  group would have had to check the DNA of  every cell in the growing plasticize a  group of cells that exists from days  five to nine post fertilization that  eventually becomes the embryo given that  they would have had to destroy the  plasticity to test all the cell's a  clear logistical problem exists in  trying to qualify the mutation exists in  all cells accordingly her and his group  only checked a number of cells from the  plasti cyst this means both twins might  have a condition called mosaic ism where  the deletion only occurs in a subset of  their cells this means that the  different cells in their body have  different DNA  in this context the effects of this  condition are completely unstudied  finally the gene that hurt took a mat  has also been reported to have a role in  learning a link between the activity of  the ccr5 gene product and the dampening  down of the brain's ability to form new  neural connections has been previously  described in mice models theoretically  there is a possibility that the induced  deletion could have a positive effect on  the twins ability to learn right now  there are far too many unknowns to make  an accurate prediction on what if any  effect this experiment will have on the  two twins and there is an even bigger  question about what effect the  announcement will have on the progress  of the field complicating this mess is  the fact that this study did not go in  front of an adequate EDX approval board  and the default Chinese laws prohibits  any kind of follow-up with twins because  of this we will likely never know what  will become of lulu and nana doctor who  has stated that he plans to publish the  work in a peer-reviewed journal but  given the fact that he has gone m.i.a  for almost two months now the scientific  community may never have an opportunity  to properly review and digest the impact  of his work so where do we go from here  there is no doubt that genetic  engineering is a valuable tool that can  potentially safely increase human  well-being and productivity it's not  unlikely that plunging into these  uncharted waters unaccounted and without  approval may have a chilling effect on  the proper utilization and development  of this technology perhaps until a  consensus on the way forward is  established this is a good thing  thankfully the World Health Organization  has stepped up to take a moderating role  in the process and are establishing a  working group to establish clear  guidelines we need these guidelines  because we stepped into a new era of  Medicine one where the genetic  modification of humans is not only a  possibility but an increasingly real  option humans have long sought to  improve themselves through technology  from the printing press to the Internet  these inventions exist to expand our  knowledge and inform us maybe one day  we'll be able to alter our genes to make  ourselves smarter but in the meantime  were  ready surrounded by tools for this like  watching educational videos on YouTube  are watching in-depth tutorials and  classes like these ones you'll find on  Skillshare Skillshare gives you the  perfect place to start learning with  over 25,000 classes in a huge range of  topics ranging from creative skills like  painting and music lessons to technical  skills like coding with professional and  understandable classes that follow a  clear learning curve you can dive in and  start learning how to do the work you  love a premium membership begins around  $10 a month for unlimited access to all  courses but the first 1,000 people to  sign up with this link will get their  first two months for free so ask  yourself right now what skill have you  been putting off learning or project  have you been dreaming of completing  what you aren't sure if you've the  skills to do it why not start right now  and sign up the skill share using the  link below to get your first two months  for free you have nothing to lose and a  valuable life skill to gain as usual  thanks for watching and thank you to all  my patreon supporters if you'd like to  see more from me the links to my  Instagram Twitter discord server and  subreddit are below  [Music]

